  <p>Gigaflush is free software, licensed under the <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>GNU General Public License v3.0 or later</a>. The GPL governs your use, modification, and redistribution of the code, including code in builds you purchase.</p>
  <p>The Gigaflush name and logo are not licensed under the GPL. Modified versions you distribute must use a different name and icon.</p>

  <h2>Purchases</h2>
  <p>A purchase gets you signed, ready-to-run builds for the platform you bought, delivered through your Polar library, including new versions made available there. Orders are processed by <a href="https://polar.sh">Polar</a> as merchant of record; Polar's terms of service apply to the checkout and payment.</p>

  <h2>Refunds</h2>
  <p>If Gigaflush doesn't work for you, email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a> within 30 days of purchase with your order email, and we'll refund you.</p>

  <h2>Your files</h2>
  <p>Gigaflush permanently deletes the folders you confirm; it does not move them to the Trash. Review every path before removal and keep backups of anything you can't recreate. Recognized folders are normally regenerated by your package manager or build tool, but anything you stored inside them by hand will be lost.</p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>As stated in the GPL, the software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, to the extent permitted by applicable law. To the same extent, we are not liable for data loss or other damages arising from its use.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
